 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * System-PM constraint layer: declare which SoC power states cut power to the
 * comparator, so the PM policy must not pick one of them while something holds a
 * pm_policy_device_power_lock on the node. Layered on top of app.overlay.
 *
 * On MCXN947, boards/nxp/frdm_mcxn947/board.c enables the CMP0 analog block for
 * *active* mode only -- it calls SPC_EnableActiveModeAnalogModules() and never
 * SPC_EnableLowPowerModeAnalogModules() -- so the comparator loses its analog bias
 * from deep sleep downwards. Plain 'sleep' only gates the core clock and is therefore
 * not listed. Adjust per real project characterization; a design that sets
 * enable-stop-mode and picks a FRO_16K/XTAL32K function clock keeps the comparator
 * alive in stop modes and would list fewer states here.
 */

&lpcmp0 {
	zephyr,disabling-power-states = <&deepsleep &powerdown &deeppowerdown>;
};
